      "goal": "Extract the Parser's configuration and tracking responsibility (settings, error tracking, position tracking, tag set, and max depth) into a new ParserConfig class to reduce Parser's public API surface and overall method count.",
      "expected_impact": {
        "primary_metric": "public_methods",
        "public_methods_moved": 11,
        "total_methods_moved": 11,
        "loc_reduction_expected": "medium",
        "rationale": "The Parser currently exposes many public getters/setters and fields related to parse configuration and error/position tracking. These form a cohesive responsibility (configuration/tracking). Moving them into a dedicated ParserConfig class consolidates related state and behavior, replacing many separate public methods with a single config accessor. This reduces the target class public method count (primary goal) and the total method count and LOC within Parser by centralizing configuration logic."
